  message: "RE-CHECK 2026-11-02 on dev ae02786fca (WI-jomik acceptance sweep, after PR #2004: shared resolvers no longer guess among tied candidates; PR #2006: a Rust method call never binds a free function). VERDICT: STILL_REPRODUCES. Repro run: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_B/surid, a small Go fixture of the filed shapes in place of cert-manager. pkg/logs has func WithResource, struct Widget and type Option; srv has func NewServer. app/app.go has corev1.SchemeGroupVersion.WithResource(\"secrets\"), corev1.SchemeGroupVersion.Widget(), tmpltext.New(\"\").Option(...) and smtp.NewServer(nil) (import github.com/emersion/go-smtp). Run with hypergumbo survey.. Observed: Use -> go:pkg/logs/logs.go:3-3:WithResource:function L11 conf=0.85 res=True call_construct=method. UseStruct -> go:pkg/logs/logs.go:5-5:Widget:struct L15 conf=0.85 res=True call_construct=method. UseSmtp -> go:srv/s.go:3-3:NewServer:function L23 conf=0.85 res=True. UseResult -> go:text/template:0-0:Option:external_symbol res=False, which is correct: it does not bind the repo Option type.. Note: Short ID WI-surid is ambiguous. I picked the Go call-shape item, which shares mechanism with WI-dibiv. WI-surid-saruf (TLA+ dep) is status done and was not judged. The external-call-result shape (alertmanager tmpltext.New(\"\").Option -> repo Option type) did not reproduce in my mini-fixture, but the alertmanager original was not run, so that sub-shape is unverified rather than fixed. Corpus counts (cert-manager 306/11/158) were not re-measured: small fixtures only. Fixtures: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_*/."  # cecb
